# wx16 - 16x16 multi-colour weather icons.
#
# These are a "font" rather than a separate bitmap format on purpose: the icon
# set then reuses fontgen, the glyph blitter, and the clip logic with no extra
# code. The icon widget maps a WMO weather code to a category 0-9 and draws the
# matching character.
#
# Four colour planes, in palette order, each drawn as its own colour by the
# icon widget when the layout supplies a "colors" array:
#
#   '#'  sun / lightning        (the widget's primary colour)
#   '*'  cloud / fog            (cloud colour)
#   '~'  rain / drizzle         (precipitation colour)
#   '+'  snow                   (flake colour)
#
# A layout without "colors" tints every plane with its single colour, so the
# icons remain legible from any layout that predates palettes.
#
#   48 '0'  clear          51 '3'  overcast      54 '6'  rain      57 '9'  storm
#   49 '1'  fair           52 '4'  fog           55 '7'  snow
#   50 '2'  cloudy         53 '5'  drizzle       56 '8'  showers
#   58 ':'  water drop      (precipitation marker)

@name     wx16
@role     icons
@planes   4
@height   16
@baseline 16
@gap      0
@family   wx
@smooth   yes
@downscale yes

# clear: full sun with eight rays
48
  |................|
  |.......##.......|
  |.......##.......|
  |..##........##..|
  |..##..####..##..|
  |......####......|
  |....########....|
  |##.##########.##|
  |##.##########.##|
  |....########....|
  |......####......|
  |..##..####..##..|
  |..##........##..|
  |.......##.......|
  |.......##.......|
  |................|

